1075 #edb/ref 17592186513394 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513414 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513411 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513414 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513414 1077 "selection" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513414 1078 #edb/ref 17592186513389 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513414 1079 #uuid "f242afd2-b1c2-5dee-b46d-cefed40a3bd8" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513415 1080 "images/ab/ab0520786330580814795f0b26baf8b1fea0f8eef5d412ee58a924d22033d6bf.png" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513415 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513415 1083 #uuid "f2d169b7-faae-5c13-bf66-8b8a0860caf9" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513416 1080 "(0,-8)" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513416 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513416 1083 #uuid "f50698c5-ac01-5deb-86f7-eb5a03f596c0" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513417 1080 "images/f3/f3438d876b653dd7aece26625ecea04ac3d40faa04bb379f583b5e208ccfaec2.png" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513417 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513417 1083 #uuid "f55c5f13-8205-5ce7-b307-71d75cff31d9" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513418 1068 #edb/ref 17592186513374 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513418 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513418 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=6.5({3}^{x})-0.5?$" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513418 1072 #uuid "fb0cfba4-eeeb-5c5b-b7db-97b99d0eccb2" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513418 1074 "First, we plot the graph of $y={3}^{x}:$\n\n![](images/6a/6a7938d23d1de5e91d734afd9a930d1d8cc1f82407dd484177d3f7852a27a915.png)\n\nNext, we plot the graph of $y=6.5({3}^{x}).$ To do this, we scale the graph above by a factor of $6.5.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,6.5),$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/8f/8f8c99a7d9b4ea251c25da35ffce56ca1a8e94225dcab7075bf687e192ad0a09.png)\n\nFinally, we plot the graph of $y=6.5({3}^{x})-0.5.$ To do this, we shift the above graph $0.5$ units down. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,6.5)$ to $(0,6),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-0.5.$\n\n![](images/74/748d7970553a8d054c415882a443e61bcd2f858da92079d537bc3574e36c28b9.png)" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513419 1068 #edb/ref 17592186513395 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513419 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513419 1071 "For the curve $y=6({10}^{x})-8,$ find the point of intersection with the $y$-axis." 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513419 1072 #uuid "ff4b88d8-da28-5f54-8746-3c0f00566a0c" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513419 1074 "**Method 1**\n\n- For the curve $y={10}^{x},$ the point of intersection with the $y$-axis is $(0,1).$\n\n- For the scaled function $y=6({10}^{x}),$ the $y$-coordinate becomes\n\n$$\ny=6\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- Finally, after a vertical shift of $8$ units down, we get a point with the $y$-coordinate\n\n$$\ny=6-8=-2.\n$$\n\n**Method 2** \n\nTo find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6({10}^{0})-8 \\\\  & =6\\cdot 1-8 \\\\  & =6-8 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=6({10}^{x})-8,$ intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-2).$" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513420 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186087823.py" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true] [17592186513420 1169 #uuid "35bd8dd3-54c5-5fe0-8635-7b694fdfe873" 13194139535538 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"023974b6-d52e-54a2-a035-bc3d44ad09c2" 17592186513350 "052c68d3-8c32-5683-b862-d94a7bb06d65" 17592186513351 "082d9271-1b37-5ab5-be6d-7707a2094f66" 17592186513352 "09f7fd95-5b85-572f-83fb-d96bf9a